Rule 2 (Axes tuple must have length 2, with both axes being positive and within the rank of their respective tensors, and the sizes along these axes must match)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ v_1[0] > 0 ∧ v_1[1] > 0 ∧ v_1[0] < ndim(v_2) ∧ v_1[1] < ndim(v_3) ∧ shape(v_2, v_1[0]) = shape(v_3, v_1[1])
>>
Rule 3 (The batch dimension (axis 0) of both input tensors must have the same size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 4 (Both input tensors must have a rank of at least 2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 5 (The input tensors must have the same data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
