Rule 7 (The dot product axis cannot be the batch axis 0 and must be within the bounds of both tensors, with identical sizes along the resolved axis)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 < ndim(v_2) ∧ v_1 < ndim(v_3) ∧ shape(v_2, v_1) = shape(v_3, v_1)) ∨ (v_1 < 0 ∧ v_1 > 0 - ndim(v_2) ∧ v_1 > 0 - ndim(v_3) ∧ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) + v_1) = shape(v_3, ndim(v_3) + v_1))
>>
Rule 8 (If axes is a tuple of two integers, both must be valid non-zero axes for their respective tensors, and the size along these resolved axes must match)
